  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'dark tourism' has gained popularity in recent years. It refers to the practice of visiting places associated with death and disaster, such as war zones, natural disasters, or historical tragedies. Proponents argue that these trips provide a unique opportunity for personal growth and self-reflection, allowing tourists to confront their own mortality and appreciate the value of life.\n\nCritics, however, claim that dark tourism is nothing more than voyeurism, where visitors exploit the suffering of others for entertainment purposes. They point out that many of these sites are still active or have a strong emotional resonance for local communities, making it insensitive to visit them.\n\nDespite these concerns, dark tourism has become a thriving industry, with tour operators offering guided visits to places like Chernobyl, Pompeii, and the Titanic wreck site. The question remains whether this trend is a reflection of humanity's fascination with mortality or its insensitivity towards others' suffering.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Dark tourism provides an opportunity for personal growth and self-reflection.\", \"Dark tourism is a reflection of humanity's fascination with mortality.\", \"Critics argue that dark tourism is voyeurism, while proponents see it as a way to appreciate life.\", \"The article discusses the concept of dark tourism without taking a stance.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Critics argue that dark tourism is voyeurism, while proponents see it as a way to appreciate life.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the reasons why critics are opposed to dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"It allows tourists to confront their own mortality.\", \"It exploits the suffering of others for entertainment purposes.\", \"It provides a unique opportunity for personal growth and self-reflection.\", \"It is too expensive.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"It exploits the suffering of others for entertainment purposes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'dark tourism' refer to?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Visiting places associated with death and disaster.\", \"Taking guided tours in natural environments.\", \"Exploring historical sites without a guide.\", \"Traveling to countries with different cultures.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Visiting places associated with death and disaster.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What can be inferred about the author's attitude towards dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The author is a strong supporter of dark tourism.\", \"The author is neutral and presents both sides of the argument.\", \"The author is critical of dark tourism, but acknowledges its popularity.\", \"The author does not take a stance on the issue.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The author is critical of dark tourism, but acknowledges its popularity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is one of the consequences of the growing popularity of dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Local communities are able to benefit financially from tourism.\", \"Tourists are able to appreciate the value of life by confronting their own mortality.\", \"The industry has become a thriving business, with tour operators offering guided visits.\", \"Critics have been silenced by the popularity of dark tourism.\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The industry has become a thriving business, with tour operators offering guided visits.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
